{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs68CW9D1fUUZCLe5ts6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The nightly report slowdown is fixed. The full suite passes (3 tests, 0.11s) with the fix in place.\n\n**Root cause:** `dedupe_rows` in `reporting/dedupe.py` tracked seen event IDs in a list (`seen_ids = []`) and checked `r.event_id in seen_ids` for every row. Each check scans the whole list, so the cost grows with the square of the row count. The refactor wanted to keep first-occurrence order and swapped the set for a list. `build_report` calls it on every run.\n\n**Fix:** `seen_ids` is now a set, so lookups are constant time. The loop still appends to `out` in input order, so first-occurrence order is unchanged. The output and public API are the same.\n\n**Regression test:** `tests/test_dedupe_perf.py` has two tests.\n- `test_dedupe_keeps_first_occurrence_order` checks that duplicates are dropped and the first occurrence's order is kept.\n- `test_dedupe_scales_linearly` runs 60k rows (20k unique) through `dedupe_rows` and `build_report` and asserts it finishes in under 2 seconds.\n\nI reverted the fix temporarily to confirm the scaling test catches the problem. It failed at about 12.6s against the 2s limit, and passes with the fix.\n\nThe timing assertion could be flaky on a very slow or loaded machine, though the margin is large.\n\nI did not commit anything. The `.pyc` files under `__pycache__` are tracked in this repo and show as modified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12914,"cache_read_input_tokens":37274,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12914},"output_tokens":504,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45273193-94dc-4e02-83f5-5b